.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt TZSETUP 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm tzsetup
.Nd set the local time zone
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl nr
.Op Ar zone
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility sets the system's local time zone by making
.Pa /etc/localtime
a symbolic link to a file of the time zone database in
.Pa /usr/share/zoneinfo .
.Pp
With a
.Ar zone ,
such as
.Ql Europe/Berlin
or
.Ql UTC ,
.Nm
checks that the zone's file exists and is a valid
.Xr tzfile 5 ,
then replaces the link.
The new link is created beside the old one and renamed over it, so
.Pa /etc/localtime
is never missing, and it is left unchanged if anything fails.
.Pp
Without a
.Ar zone ,
.Nm
shows numbered menus on the terminal: first the regions of the database, and
UTC, then the zones within the chosen region, each with its country and the
area it covers.
Enter a number to choose,
.Ql b
to go back to the regions, or
.Ql q
to quit without changing anything.
.Nm
asks for confirmation before setting the zone.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Do nothing; print the command that would have been run.
.It Fl r
Read the zone's name from the current
.Pa /etc/localtime
link and create the link again, checking the zone's file anew.
Useful after the database has been updated.
.El
.Pp
Running programs follow the change within a second: the C library checks
.Pa /etc/localtime
again at most once a second when converting local time, as long as
.Ev TZ
is unset.
Without
.Pa /etc/localtime ,
local time is UTC.
The
.Ev TZ
environment variable overrides
.Pa /etc/localtime
for a process, with a zone name or a POSIX rule such as
.Ql EST5EDT .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/zoneinfo/zone1970.tab -compact
.It Pa /etc/localtime
The link to the local time zone.
.It Pa /usr/share/zoneinfo
The time zone database.
.It Pa /usr/share/zoneinfo/zone1970.tab
The zones offered by the menus.
.It Pa /usr/share/zoneinfo/iso3166.tab
Country names for the menus.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Set the local time zone to Central European Time:
.Pp
.Dl # tzsetup Europe/Berlin
.Pp
Refresh the link after installing a newer database:
.Pp
.Dl # tzsetup -r
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr date 1 ,
.Xr tzfile 5 ,
.Xr syslogd 8 ,
.Xr zdump 8 ,
.Xr zic 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 2.0.5 .
OxideBSD's was written from scratch; it keeps
.Fx Ns 's
name and options but offers numbered menus instead of
.Xr dialog 1 .
